1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,707
Meet the McKinley assistant,

2
00:00:01,707 --> 00:00:06,464
a prototype that helps residents and future
residents get answers at any hour.

3
00:00:06,911 --> 00:00:11,945
It runs on made-up data, and it tells people up
front that they're talking to an AI.

4
00:00:12,396 --> 00:00:16,193
First, someone looking for an apartment
taps: I need a place soon.

5
00:00:16,643 --> 00:00:19,843
The assistant asks only what it
needs. Which community?

6
00:00:20,293 --> 00:00:21,253
Which days?

7
00:00:22,433 --> 00:00:23,713
And what time of day?

8
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:28,485
Then it shows a summary to check.
Nothing is sent until they say so.

9
00:00:28,936 --> 00:00:32,264
One tap, and the tour request is
saved for the leasing team.

10
00:00:32,716 --> 00:00:36,769
Now let's sign in as Marisol, a
resident at Heron Lake Apartments.

11
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:40,633
Her air conditioning has stopped
cooling again, and she's upset.

12
00:00:41,084 --> 00:00:43,902
The assistant can see her
earlier repair visits,

13
00:00:43,902 --> 00:00:48,657
so it doesn't make her troubleshoot again. It
flags a repeat issue for a manager.

14
00:00:49,107 --> 00:00:52,733
It asks one question: may maintenance
come in if she's not home?

15
00:00:53,184 --> 00:00:57,130
Everything else comes from her account, and
each line shows where it came from.

16
00:00:57,581 --> 00:01:00,525
She sends it, and gets a
reference number right away.

17
00:01:00,976 --> 00:01:03,408
She can check on all her requests at any time.

18
00:01:03,858 --> 00:01:05,180
Safety comes first.

19
00:01:07,714 --> 00:01:11,703
When Theo writes that he smells gas, the
assistant skips everything else.

20
00:01:12,153 --> 00:01:14,510
It tells him to get outside and call 911,

21
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:17,614
and puts an urgent note at the
top of the staff queue.

22
00:01:18,064 --> 00:01:20,133
Residents can also write in Spanish.

23
00:01:23,694 --> 00:01:27,000
Valeria gets the same careful
help, in her own language.

24
00:01:28,411 --> 00:01:30,459
And it protects residents' information.

25
00:01:32,282 --> 00:01:36,013
When someone claiming to be a
contractor asks for a gate code,

26
00:01:36,013 --> 00:01:39,684
it politely declines and passes a
note to the office instead.

27
00:01:40,134 --> 00:01:42,672
Behind the scenes, staff have
their own console.

28
00:01:43,122 --> 00:01:47,900
Saved requests lists everything the assistant
prepared, with urgent items first.

29
00:01:48,351 --> 00:01:52,368
The conversation inspector shows each
step: what the person wrote,

30
00:01:52,368 --> 00:01:54,559
what the assistant decided, and why.

31
00:01:55,009 --> 00:02:00,027
The McKinley assistant: quicker answers for
residents, clearer handoffs for staff,

32
00:02:00,027 --> 00:02:01,067
and safety first.

33
00:02:01,518 --> 00:02:04,132
Next, we would connect it to McKinley's real

34
00:02:04,132 --> 00:02:07,875
systems and keep testing its safety
rules. Thanks for watching.

